:Namespace LiveDemo
⍝ Combined Jarvis demo (JSON mode): Server-Sent Events, WebSockets and an ordinary JSON endpoint
⍝ See README.md.
⍝
⍝ Three channels, one server:
⍝   SSE  (one-way, server → client)  GET /feed   - a live feed: a "tick" event every second with the time and
⍝                                                  the current client counts; EventSource in the browser
⍝   WebSocket (two-way)              ws:// … /    - a shared chat: the browser sends {"name":…,"text":…} and the
⍝                                                  server broadcasts a "chat" message to every WebSocket client
⍝   JSON (request/response)          POST /stats - returns the current counts and server time
⍝
⍝ The Ticker thread (started by Initialize) shows application code pushing SSE events from outside any request;
⍝ the WebSocket hooks show two-way messaging and broadcasting with WsSend.

    (⎕IO ⎕ML)←1 1

    Server←⍬          ⍝ the Jarvis instance, set by Initialize
    WsClients←⍬       ⍝ conx names of the open WebSocket connections
    TickId←0          ⍝ id of the latest SSE tick; browsers send it back as Last-Event-ID when they reconnect
    TickerThread←⍬
    Stopping←0

    fmtTime←{,'ZI2,<:>,ZI2,<:>,ZI2'⎕FMT 1 3⍴3↑3↓⍵}   ⍝ ⎕TS → 'hh:mm:ss'
    trim←{⍵/⍨(∨\b)∧⌽∨\⌽b←' '≠⍵}                        ⍝ remove leading and trailing blanks

    ∇ r←Initialize server
    ⍝ AppInitFn: remember the server and start the SSE ticker thread
      Server←server
      Stopping←0
      WsClients←⍬
      TickId←0
      TickerThread←Ticker&1
      r←0
    ∇

    ∇ r←Shutdown
    ⍝ AppCloseFn: stop the ticker thread
      Stopping←1
      ⎕TKILL TickerThread
      r←0
    ∇

⍝ ─── SSE: the live feed ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←feed req;last;msg
    ⍝ SSE endpoint function, called once for each new client after the stream has started
      last←req.GetHeader'last-event-id' ⍝ a reconnecting browser tells us the last tick it saw
      msg←'Connected to the live feed'
      :If ~0∊⍴last ⋄ msg,←'. Last tick you saw was #',last ⋄ :EndIf
      {}req Server.SendSSE msg ⍝ plain text → one unnamed "data:" event, to this client only
      r←0                      ⍝ 0 keeps the stream open
    ∇

    ∇ Ticker interval;conxs;data
    ⍝ every interval seconds, broadcast a "tick" event (with an id) to every SSE client of /feed
      :While ~Stopping
          {}⎕DL interval
          TickId+←1
          :If ~0∊⍴conxs←Server.SSEConnections'feed'
              (data←⎕NS'').(time sseClients wsClients)←(fmtTime ⎕TS)(≢conxs)(≢WsClients)
              {}conxs Server.SendSSE('tick'TickId)Server.FormatSSE data
          :EndIf
      :EndWhile
    ∇

⍝ ─── WebSocket: the shared chat ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←WsConnect ns;msg
    ⍝ OnWsUpgradeFn: a new WebSocket connection - remember it and welcome just this client
      WsClients,←⊂ns.conx
      (msg←⎕NS'').(type text time)←'system' 'Welcome to the chat'(fmtTime ⎕TS)
      {}(ns.conx)ns.Server.WsSend msg ⍝ namespace → sent as JSON to this one client
      r←0                             ⍝ 0 keeps the connection open
    ∇

    ∇ r←WsReceive req;ns;payload;name;text;msg
    ⍝ OnWsReceiveFn: a message from a client - broadcast it to every chat client
      ns←req.##
      name text←'' ''
      :Trap 0 ⍝ ignore anything that isn't the JSON we expect
          payload←⎕JSON req.Payload
          name←40 limit payload'name'
          text←500 limit payload'text'
      :EndTrap
      :If ~0∊⍴text
          (msg←⎕NS'').(type name text time)←'chat'({0∊⍴⍵:'anonymous' ⋄ ⍵}name)text(fmtTime ⎕TS)
          Broadcast msg
      :EndIf
      r←0 ⍝ 0 keeps the connection open
    ∇

    ∇ r←WsClose ns;msg
    ⍝ OnWsCloseFn: a client left - forget it
      WsClients~←⊂ns.conx
      r←0
    ∇

    ∇ Broadcast obj;res
    ⍝ send namespace obj as JSON to every WebSocket client, dropping any that have gone away
      :If ~0∊⍴WsClients
          res←WsClients Server.WsSend obj
          WsClients/⍨←0=res ⍝ keep only the connections that accepted the message
      :EndIf
    ∇

⍝ ─── JSON: an ordinary request/response endpoint ─────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←stats payload
    ⍝ POST /stats → the current counts and server time
      (r←⎕NS'').(sseClients wsClients ticks time)←(≢Server.SSEConnections'feed')(≢WsClients)TickId(fmtTime ⎕TS)
    ∇

⍝ ─── helper ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←max limit(ns name)
    ⍝ the trimmed text of field name in namespace ns, at most max characters ('' if it's missing)
      r←''
      :Trap 0
          r←trim,⍕ns⍎name
      :EndTrap
      r←(max⌊≢r)↑r
    ∇

:EndNamespace
